A||||4||Santa Cruzer||How do i remove the whole winshield wiper arm?||||1||
Z||000000||Santa Cruzer||07-09-2001||01:49 PM||||it's carked off how do i remove it?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Wolfhound||07-09-2001||03:05 PM||||Pry up on the outer 1/16 of the edge with a wide blade screw driver. Using a wood block fulcrum makes it easy. Make sure you don't pry on the shaft it's self.<BR>Once you try it it's obvious.||||reg||1
Z||000002||286SE'S||07-09-2001||03:26 PM||||I am not familiar with the term "carked off"<BR>but do know that attacking it with a screwdriver is the best way to cause damage.<BR>There is no place to get leverage since it is comming up throught the plastic rain shield.<BR>I suggest you get the proper tool for this. It is only a few bucks:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.bobstools.net/Store/LS65750.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.bobstools.net/Store/LS65750.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||07-09-2001||03:28 PM||||the easiest way is to slide a rivit into the hole on the wiper arm while you are holding it out from the windshield, then just lift it off -- it isn't difficult that way at all........||||reg||1
Z||000004||Carrolles||07-09-2001||04:06 PM||||Tgowens is right.  Lift up on the arm and slip a nail or rivet into the hole at the honge point.  This will hold the arm in the raised position.  Now just slide the arm assembly off the shaft.  You might have to wiggle it a bit.<P>No need for special tools or screwdrivers.<P>Later model ones have a clip that swings out to hold the arm in the raised position instead of a hole for a pin to be inserted.<p>[This message has been edited by Carrolles (edited 07-09-2001).]||||reg||1
